-- title:
--   Invariant series are uniquely series in invariant generators
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring, and let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule`: a two-dimensional formal group law $F = X.F$ over $B$ together with a commutativity hypothesis, an action `act` of `Zp2 p` and a series `varpi`, all of these being law endomorphisms of $F$ and subject to the unit, multiplicativity, additivity, $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\mathrm{Frob}(a)]\circ\varpi$ identities; only the law $F$, viewed as a pair of power series in $B[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$, enters the statement. Let $I$ be an ideal of $A = B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ such that $A/I$ is a finite free $B$-module and such that for some $q$ both $x_1^q$ and $x_2^q$ lie in $I$. Call an element $v\in A$ invariant if $v(F(x,y)) - v(x)$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$ generated by the image of $I$ under $x\mapsto y$. Assume $u = (u_1,u_2)$ is a pair of invariant elements of $A$ with zero constant term which generates $I$, and let $w\in A$ be invariant. Then there is exactly one $W\in B[\![T_1,T_2]\!]$ with $W(u_1,u_2) = w$.
--
--   This is the closing step in Lubin's description of the quotient of a formal group law by a finite subgroup: once the subgroup ideal $I$ is generated by two invariant series $u_1,u_2$ without constant term, the invariants of $A$ are precisely the power series in $u_1,u_2$, and uniquely so, which identifies $B[\![T_1,T_2]\!]$ with the ring of invariants and hence makes $u$ a coordinate system on the quotient. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_invariant_coordinates_of_subgroup_ideal`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_cover_invariant_coordinates_of_subgroup_ideal).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_existsUnique_subst_eq_of_invariant_of_span_range_eq_of_free.lean

